cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroSim GPU in academic work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "NeuroSim GPU: GPU-first sparse neural simulation with persistent synaptic currents"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype of a fixed-topology sparse neural simulator. It treats the
  neural core as a sparse linear-algebra workload (O(BM + BN) per tick) and adds
  bounded-error persistent-current event propagation, regional dopamine chemistry,
  eligibility-based three-factor plasticity, delayed communication and a
  multi-rate scheduler, with native fused CUDA kernels and measured performance
  and accuracy reports.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - computational neuroscience
  - sparse neural simulation
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - spiking neural network
  - dopamine
  - eligibility trace
  - event-driven simulation

authors:
